window.portfolioTranslations = {"en":{"languageLabel":"Language","navAbout":"About","navWork":"Work","navContact":"Contact","intro":"HELLO, I’M TAHA","heroTitle":"Taha Chelly.<br><span>Software engineer.</span><br>Builder at heart.","heroDescription":"I build thoughtful AI-powered products, connecting reliable systems with intuitive user experiences.","connect":"Let’s connect","github":"GitHub","currentlyAt":"Currently at <a href=\"#work\">SpeakDuo</a>","role":"Software Engineer","portraitNote":"Turning ideas into real-world experiences","aboutKicker":"A LITTLE CONTEXT","aboutTitle":"The person behind the code.","aboutText":"I’m Taha Chelly, a software engineer based in Sfax, Tunisia. I enjoy the whole journey of building a product: connecting a clear interface, a reliable backend, and the intelligence that makes it useful.","aboutDetail":"I’m a software engineering graduate with experience building Python backends, REST APIs, and AI-powered applications using FastAPI, SQL, and Docker. I’ve contributed to production features at SpeakDuo and built end-to-end AI projects. I’m seeking a full-time Python developer role to build reliable backend services and grow in AI engineering.","tagFullStack":"Full-stack development","tagAI":"AI applications","tagRealtime":"Real-time experiences","workKicker":"WHAT I’M WORKING ON","workTitle":"Building with purpose.","current":"Current","workHeading":"Helping people learn languages.<br>One conversation at a time.","workDescription":"I work across SpeakDuo’s backend, web app, and voice agents—building live translation, speech feedback, interactive activities, and personalized practice.","remote":"Remote","toolkitTitle":"Some tools I work with","contactKicker":"GOOD THINGS START WITH A CONVERSATION","contactTitle":"Let’s build something<br><span>worth talking about.</span>","footerLine":"Built with care. Always evolving.","backToTop":"Back to top ↑","navProjects":"Projects","projectsKicker":"SELECTED PROJECTS","projectsTitle":"Ideas brought to life.","viewProject":"Explore project ↗","projectCategory":"AUDIO · AI · WEB","projectSummary":"Discover who is reciting and which verse you’re hearing. An audio recognition app for Qur’an recitation, with live listening and file uploads.","backProjects":"← All projects","liveDemo":"Try the live demo","sourceCode":"View on GitHub","screenshotsKicker":"A LOOK INSIDE","screenshotsTitle":"Two ways to explore a recitation.","reciterCaption":"Reciter recognition — upload audio or listen live.","verseCaption":"Verse discovery — find the surah and ayah from a recitation.","approachKicker":"BEHIND THE EXPERIENCE","approachTitle":"From sound to a meaningful match.","reciterTitle":"Recognize the reciter","reciterDetail":"An ECAPA-TDNN model creates a voice embedding. ONNX Runtime runs inference, then cosine similarity ranks matches against profiles for 20 reciters.","verseTitle":"Find the verse","verseDetail":"A Quran-tuned Whisper model transcribes the Arabic audio. Normalized text is matched against 6,236 verses to find likely surah and ayah matches.","contextTitle":"Listen for more context","contextDetail":"When a verse match is ambiguous, progressive listening gathers more audio context. Uncertain results stay marked as uncertain.","stackKicker":"BUILT WITH","stackTitle":"The technology behind it.","frontendDetail":"Frontend: React 19 and TypeScript, built with Vite and Tailwind CSS 4. Browser microphone capture and file uploads connect to the API.","backendDetail":"Backend: Python and FastAPI, with WebSockets for live reciter recognition. ONNX Runtime handles speaker embeddings; faster-whisper and CTranslate2 handle verse transcription.","deployDetail":"Delivery: Docker containers on Render, with Nginx serving the frontend. GitHub Actions checks the backend and frontend before deploying affected services.","tryTitle":"Hear it. Discover it.","qafiyaCategory":"LANGUAGE · POETRY · AI","qafiyaSummary":"An Arabic poetry workshop for classical meter, rhyme, readable scansion, and local vocalization.","qafiyaCaptionDesk":"Writing desk — choose a classical meter and rhyme letter, then inspect the verse.","qafiyaCaptionMobile":"Responsive Arabic-first poetry analysis on mobile.","qafiyaApproachTitle":"From a written verse to its rhythm.","qafiyaAnalysisTitle":"Analyze classical meter","qafiyaAnalysisDetail":"Check Arabic verses against 16 classical meters with PyArud. Explore the صدر and عجز, binary scansion, feet, and the requested rawi.","qafiyaTashkeelTitle":"Complete vocalization locally","qafiyaTashkeelDetail":"A bundled 4.8 MB libtashkeel ONNX model fills missing vowel marks on the CPU. Supplied vowels remain authoritative; analysis does not call an LLM.","qafiyaDraftTitle":"Drafting is experimental","qafiyaDraftDetail":"An optional provider adapter drafts poems and targets revisions at failed verses while preserving accepted text. Generation is currently disabled on the public demo.","qafiyaFrontend":"Frontend: React 19, TypeScript, and Vite, with a responsive Arabic RTL interface.","qafiyaBackend":"Backend: Python 3.12, FastAPI, PyArud, NumPy, and CPU ONNX Runtime. A single worker shares a bounded inference session.","qafiyaDeploy":"Hosting: Cloudflare Pages frontend and Render Docker API. GitHub Actions checks the frontend, backend, and production container.","qafiyaTryTitle":"Explore meter and rhyme.","generationPaused":"Analysis is available in the live demo. AI generation is currently disabled.","downloadCV":"Download CV","contactIntent":"I’m looking for a full-time Python developer role, building reliable backend services and AI applications. If that fits your team, let’s talk.","employmentDates":"Software Engineer · Jul 2026 — Present","internshipDates":"Previously: end-of-studies internship at SpeakDuo · Jan — Jul 2026.","achievementFeedback":"Developed multilingual grammar and pronunciation feedback, lesson generation, and personalized practice for the production platform.","achievementPractice":"Built vocabulary tracking, spaced repetition exercises, and Elo-based CEFR assessment to support adaptive learning.","achievementVoice":"Implemented a multilingual LiveKit voice interview agent and optimized speech recognition for real-time captions using voice activity detection.","achievementMultiplayer":"Delivered AI chat, personal grammar practice, and synchronized multiplayer learning activities across the backend and web app.","writingKicker":"Engineering notebook","writingTitle":"Technical decisions, explained.","decisionsKicker":"CHALLENGES & TRADEOFFS","decisionsTitle":"Why it works this way.","readNote":"Read the engineering note","cvFormat":"PDF · 129 KB","story0Title":"When an audio match needs more context","story0Summary":"Separating speaker recognition from verse discovery, and making uncertainty part of the listening flow.","story0Section0Title":"Two questions, two pipelines","story0Section0Text":"Recognizing a voice and recognizing words are different problems. Quranic Shazam uses ECAPA-TDNN speaker embeddings with ONNX Runtime to rank 20 reciter profiles. Verse discovery instead uses a Quran-tuned Whisper model, normalizes the Arabic transcript, and matches it against 6,236 verses. The speaker model is pretrained; it is not fine-tuned on Qur’an recordings.","story0Section1Title":"Ask for context before claiming certainty","story0Section1Text":"A short recitation can fit more than one verse. Progressive listening adds audio context up to a 60-second limit, while ambiguous results remain marked as uncertain. This trades a longer listening window for more context instead of forcing an early answer.","story0Section2Title":"Keep inference away from the event loop","story0Section2Text":"Model inference runs off the asynchronous API event loop. Uploads are capped at 25 MB, with separate audio-duration limits for recognition modes. These bounds make expensive requests finite while the API supports uploads and live microphone sessions.","story0Section3Title":"Measure a defined task","story0Section3Text":"The September 5, 2026 offline evaluation reports 97.31% top-1 and 99.10% top-3 reciter recognition across 781 held-out clips, using disjoint profile and evaluation surahs. Those results describe that reciter benchmark; they do not measure verse recognition or guarantee performance on arbitrary microphones, noise, or recordings.","story1Title":"Arabic prosody on a small CPU server","story1Summary":"A 4.8 MB vocalization model, preserved vowel marks, and explicit limits on what automated analysis can claim.","story1Section0Title":"Fit the model to the hosting budget","story1Section0Text":"Qafiya pairs PyArud’s classical prosody analysis with a bundled approximately 4.8 MB libtashkeel ONNX model. Vocalization runs locally on the CPU without PyTorch, Transformers, a GPU, or an external model server. A single Uvicorn worker shares a bounded, serialized inference session, keeping model copies and simultaneous inference under control.","story1Section1Title":"Preserve the author’s text","story1Section1Text":"Existing vowel marks remain authoritative. Automatic vocalization fills missing marks and discloses changes; the interface shows the analyzed text while retaining the original input. The distinction matters because scansion depends on pronunciation, and a predicted vowel can change the result.","story1Section2Title":"Test the container, then state the limits","story1Section2Text":"The documented local whole-ASGI workload ran the production image under a 512 MiB RAM and 0.1 CPU cap, peaking at 142.55 MiB process RSS without an out-of-memory failure. This is evidence for a bounded workload, not a guarantee under arbitrary public traffic. In a separate 12-verse vocalization sample, partial-source meter matches improved from 2/12 to 10/12; fully unvocalized input reached only 2/12.","story1Section3Title":"Keep repair bounded and sound text intact","story1Section3Text":"The experimental drafting flow checks meter and the requested rawi, then revises failed verses with a bounded loop. The backend preserves accepted verses and sound hemistichs. Rawi equality is narrower than full classical rhyme validation, and machine acceptance does not certify literary quality. AI generation remains disabled in the public demo.","notebookTitle":"Engineering notebook","allNotes":"Back to all notes","noteLabel":"Engineering note","readingTime":"3 min read","articleContext":"A technical walkthrough of the implementation and evidence documented in the project repository.","contentsLabel":"On this page","sourcesTitle":"Sources & implementation","sourceReadme":"Project README","sourceEvidence":"Evaluation & evidence","exploreProject":"Explore project","continueReading":"Continue reading","writtenBy":"Written by","evidenceCaption":"Based on the project README and linked evaluations.","copyLink":"Copy link","linkCopied":"Link copied","switchDark":"Switch to dark mode","switchLight":"Switch to light mode","opensNewTab":"Opens in a new tab","technologyLabel":"Technology","contactLinksLabel":"Contact and social links","homeLabel":"Taha Chelly home","browseNotebook":"Browse the notebook","navNotebook":"Notebook","sectionLink":"Link to this section","projectSectionsLabel":"Project sections","projectScreenshots":"Screenshots","projectArchitecture":"How it works","projectDecisions":"Decisions"},"ar":{"languageLabel":"اللغة","navAbout":"نبذة","navWork":"العمل","navContact":"تواصل","intro":"أهلًا، أنا طه","heroTitle":"طه الشلي.<br><span>مهندس برمجيات.</span><br>شغوف بالبناء والتطوير.","heroDescription":"أطوّر منتجات تعتمد على AI، وأجمع فيها بين أنظمة موثوقة وتجربة استخدام واضحة وسهلة.","connect":"تواصل معي","github":"GitHub","currentlyAt":"أعمل حاليًا في <a href=\"#work\">SpeakDuo</a>","role":"مهندس برمجيات","portraitNote":"أحوّل الأفكار إلى تجارب واقعية","aboutKicker":"نبذة عنّي","aboutTitle":"من يقف وراء الكود.","aboutText":"أنا طه الشلي، مهندس برمجيات من صفاقس في تونس. أستمتع بجميع مراحل بناء المنتج، من تصميم واجهة واضحة وتطوير backend موثوق إلى إضافة ميزات ذكية تجعله مفيدًا.","aboutDetail":"أنا خريج هندسة برمجيات، ولدي خبرة في تطوير Python backends وREST APIs وتطبيقات AI باستخدام FastAPI وSQL وDocker. ساهمت في تطوير ميزات مستخدمة فعليًا في SpeakDuo وأنجزت مشاريع AI متكاملة. أبحث عن وظيفة مطوّر Python بدوام كامل لبناء خدمات backend موثوقة والتطوّر في مجال AI engineering.","tagFullStack":"تطوير Full-stack","tagAI":"تطبيقات AI","tagRealtime":"تجارب آنية","workKicker":"ما أعمل عليه","workTitle":"أبني منتجات لها معنى.","current":"حاليًا","workHeading":"أساعد الناس على تعلّم اللغات،<br>محادثةً بعد محادثة.","workDescription":"أعمل على backend منصة SpeakDuo وتطبيق الويب والوكلاء الصوتيين، وأطوّر الترجمة المباشرة والتغذية الراجعة حول الكلام والأنشطة التفاعلية والتدريب المخصّص.","remote":"عن بُعد","toolkitTitle":"بعض الأدوات التي أستخدمها","contactKicker":"كل شيء جميل يبدأ بمحادثة","contactTitle":"لنصنع شيئًا<br><span>يستحق الحديث عنه.</span>","footerLine":"بُني بعناية. ويتطور دائمًا.","backToTop":"العودة إلى الأعلى ↑","navProjects":"المشاريع","projectsKicker":"مشاريع مختارة","projectsTitle":"أفكار أصبحت واقعًا.","viewProject":"اكتشف المشروع ↗","projectCategory":"الصوت · AI · الويب","projectSummary":"تعرّف على القارئ واكتشف الآية التي تسمعها. تطبيق للتعرّف على تلاوات القرآن الكريم، بالاستماع المباشر أو رفع ملف صوتي.","backProjects":"→ جميع المشاريع","liveDemo":"جرّب التطبيق","sourceCode":"الكود على GitHub","screenshotsKicker":"صور من التطبيق","screenshotsTitle":"طريقتان لاستكشاف التلاوة.","reciterCaption":"التعرّف على القارئ: ارفع تسجيلًا أو استمع مباشرةً.","verseCaption":"اكتشاف الآيات: اعثر على السورة والآية من التلاوة.","approachKicker":"كيف يعمل","approachTitle":"من الصوت إلى التعرّف على التلاوة.","reciterTitle":"التعرّف على القارئ","reciterDetail":"يولّد نموذج ECAPA-TDNN تمثيلًا للصوت عبر ONNX Runtime. تُنفّذ عملية inference، ثم تُستخدم cosine similarity لترتيب المطابقات مع الملفات الصوتية المرجعية لـ 20 قارئًا.","verseTitle":"العثور على الآية","verseDetail":"يحوّل نموذج Whisper المخصّص للقرآن الصوت العربي إلى نص، ثم يُقارَن النص بعد توحيده مع 6236 آية لتحديد السورة والآيات المحتملة.","contextTitle":"الاستماع إلى سياق أوسع","contextDetail":"عند التباس الآية، يجمع الاستماع التدريجي مزيدًا من الصوت لفهم السياق. وتظلّ النتائج غير المؤكّدة موسومة بوضوح.","stackKicker":"التقنيات","stackTitle":"التقنيات وراء التطبيق.","frontendDetail":"Frontend: React 19 وTypeScript باستخدام Vite وTailwind CSS 4. تتصل خاصية التسجيل بميكروفون المتصفح ورفع الملفات الصوتية بالـ API.","backendDetail":"Backend: Python وFastAPI مع WebSockets للتعرّف المباشر على القارئ. يتولى ONNX Runtime حساب speaker embeddings، ويستخدم faster-whisper وCTranslate2 لتحويل التلاوة إلى نص.","deployDetail":"النشر: Docker containers على Render، مع Nginx لتقديم frontend. يتحقق GitHub Actions من backend وfrontend قبل نشر الخدمات المعدّلة.","tryTitle":"استمع. واكتشف.","qafiyaCategory":"اللغة · الشعر · AI","qafiyaSummary":"ورشة للشعر العربي تستكشف الوزن الخليلي والقافية والتقطيع وإكمال التشكيل محليًا.","qafiyaCaptionDesk":"مساحة الكتابة — اختر بحرًا ورويًا، ثم استكشف إيقاع البيت.","qafiyaCaptionMobile":"تحليل للشعر العربي بواجهة ملائمة للهاتف.","qafiyaApproachTitle":"من البيت المكتوب إلى إيقاعه.","qafiyaAnalysisTitle":"تحليل البحور الشعرية","qafiyaAnalysisDetail":"افحص الأبيات وفق 16 بحرًا خليليًا باستخدام PyArud. استكشف الصدر والعجز والتقطيع الثنائي والتفعيلات والروي المطلوب.","qafiyaTashkeelTitle":"إكمال التشكيل محليًا","qafiyaTashkeelDetail":"يُكمل نموذج libtashkeel ONNX المضمّن، بحجم 4.8 MB، الحركات الناقصة على CPU. يبقى التشكيل المزوّد معتمدًا، ولا يستدعي التحليل أي LLM.","qafiyaDraftTitle":"التوليد ما يزال تجريبيًا","qafiyaDraftDetail":"يمكن لمزوّد اختياري صياغة القصائد ومراجعة الأبيات غير المطابقة مع الحفاظ على النص السليم. التوليد معطّل حاليًا في النسخة العامة.","qafiyaFrontend":"Frontend: React 19 وTypeScript وVite، بواجهة عربية متجاوبة تدعم RTL.","qafiyaBackend":"Backend: Python 3.12 وFastAPI وPyArud وNumPy وONNX Runtime على CPU. يستخدم worker واحد جلسة inference مشتركة ومحدودة.","qafiyaDeploy":"الاستضافة: frontend على Cloudflare Pages وAPI داخل Docker على Render. يتحقق GitHub Actions من frontend وbackend وصورة production.","qafiyaTryTitle":"استكشف الوزن والقافية.","generationPaused":"تحليل الأبيات متاح في النسخة التجريبية على الموقع. التوليد باستخدام AI معطّل حاليًا.","downloadCV":"تنزيل السيرة الذاتية","contactIntent":"أبحث عن وظيفة مطوّر Python بدوام كامل لبناء خدمات backend موثوقة وتطبيقات AI. إذا كان هذا يناسب فريقكم، فلنتحدث.","employmentDates":"مهندس برمجيات · يوليو 2026 — الآن","internshipDates":"سابقًا: تدريب نهاية الدراسة في SpeakDuo · يناير — يوليو 2026.","achievementFeedback":"طوّرت تغذية راجعة متعددة اللغات حول القواعد والنطق، وميزات لتوليد الدروس والتدريب المخصّص للمنصة المستخدمة فعليًا.","achievementPractice":"بنيت تتبّع المفردات وتمارين spaced repetition وتقييم CEFR القائم على Elo لدعم التعلّم التكيّفي.","achievementVoice":"طوّرت وكيل مقابلات صوتية متعدد اللغات باستخدام LiveKit، وحسّنت speech recognition للنصوص المباشرة باستخدام voice activity detection.","achievementMultiplayer":"أنجزت ميزات AI chat والتدريب الشخصي على القواعد وأنشطة تعلّم multiplayer متزامنة عبر backend وتطبيق الويب.","writingKicker":"دفتر الهندسة","writingTitle":"شرح القرارات التقنية.","decisionsKicker":"التحديات والموازنات","decisionsTitle":"لماذا هذه الخيارات التقنية؟","readNote":"اقرأ الملاحظة الهندسية","cvFormat":"PDF · 129 KB","story0Title":"حين يحتاج التعرّف على التلاوة إلى سياق أطول","story0Summary":"فصل التعرّف على صوت القارئ عن تحديد الآية، وإظهار عدم اليقين ضمن تجربة الاستماع.","story0Section0Title":"سؤالان ومساران مختلفان","story0Section0Text":"التعرّف على صوت القارئ والتعرّف على الكلمات مسألتان مختلفتان. يستخدم Quranic Shazam تقنية speaker embeddings من ECAPA-TDNN عبر ONNX Runtime لترتيب المطابقات مع الملفات الصوتية المرجعية لـ 20 قارئًا. أما تحديد الآية فيعتمد على نموذج Whisper مكيّف للقرآن، ثم توحيد صيغة النص العربي ومقارنته بـ 6,236 آية. يُستخدم نموذج speaker embeddings بحالته pretrained، دون fine-tuning على تسجيلات قرآنية.","story0Section1Title":"جمع سياق إضافي قبل الجزم بالنتيجة","story0Section1Text":"قد يتوافق مقطع قصير مع أكثر من آية. يضيف الاستماع التدريجي سياقًا صوتيًا حتى حدّ أقصى يبلغ 60 ثانية، وتظل النتائج الملتبسة موسومة بأنها غير مؤكدة. يتيح هذا الاختيار جمع سياق أوسع مقابل وقت استماع أطول، بدلًا من فرض إجابة مبكرة.","story0Section2Title":"تنفيذ inference خارج event loop","story0Section2Text":"تُنفّذ عملية inference خارج event loop الخاصة بالـ API غير المتزامنة. يقتصر حجم الملف المرفوع على 25 MB، مع حدود زمنية للصوت تختلف بحسب وضع التعرّف. تضبط هذه الحدود تكلفة الطلبات، مع دعم رفع الملفات والاستماع المباشر عبر الميكروفون.","story0Section3Title":"قياس مهمة محددة بوضوح","story0Section3Text":"سجّل التقييم offline بتاريخ 5 سبتمبر 2026 دقة 97.31% في top-1 و99.10% في top-3 لتحديد القارئ، على 781 مقطعًا مخصّصًا للتقييم، مع فصل سور بناء الملفات الصوتية عن سور الاختبار. تصف هذه الأرقام ذلك benchmark لتحديد القارئ فقط؛ ولا تقيس تحديد الآيات أو تضمن الأداء مع مختلف الميكروفونات والضجيج والتسجيلات.","story1Title":"تحليل العَروض العربي على خادم CPU صغير","story1Summary":"نموذج تشكيل بحجم 4.8 MB، مع الحفاظ على الحركات الموجودة وتوضيح حدود التحليل الآلي.","story1Section0Title":"اختيار نموذج يناسب موارد الاستضافة","story1Section0Text":"يجمع Qafiya بين تحليل العَروض الخليلي باستخدام PyArud ونموذج libtashkeel ONNX مضمّن بحجم يقارب 4.8 MB. يعمل التشكيل محليًا على CPU دون PyTorch أو Transformers أو GPU أو خادم نماذج خارجي. يستخدم Uvicorn worker واحد جلسة inference مشتركة ومحدودة، تُنفّذ الطلبات بالتتابع لضبط عدد نسخ النموذج وعمليات التنفيذ المتزامنة.","story1Section1Title":"الحفاظ على نص الكاتب","story1Section1Text":"تبقى الحركات الموجودة في النص هي المرجع. يُكمل التشكيل التلقائي الحركات الناقصة ويوضّح التغييرات؛ وتعرض الواجهة النص الذي جرى تحليله مع إبقاء النص الأصلي متاحًا. هذا الفرق مهم لأن التقطيع يعتمد على النطق، وقد تغيّر حركة متوقّعة نتيجة التحليل.","story1Section2Title":"اختبار container وتوضيح حدود النتائج","story1Section2Text":"شغّل الاختبار المحلي الموثّق صورة production على مستوى تطبيق ASGI كاملًا، ضمن حدّ 512 MiB من RAM و0.1 CPU. بلغت ذروة process RSS مقدار 142.55 MiB دون حدوث out-of-memory. هذه نتيجة لحمل محدّد، وليست ضمانًا للأداء مع أي حجم من الزيارات العامة. وفي عيّنة منفصلة من 12 بيتًا، تحسّنت مطابقة الوزن للنصوص المشكلة جزئيًا من 2/12 إلى 10/12، بينما لم تتجاوز النصوص الخالية تمامًا من علامات التشكيل 2/12.","story1Section3Title":"حصر المراجعة والحفاظ على الأجزاء السليمة","story1Section3Text":"يفحص workflow التجريبي الوزن والروي المطلوب، ثم يراجع الأبيات غير المطابقة ضمن حلقة محدودة. يحافظ backend على الأبيات المقبولة والأشطر السليمة. تطابق الروي أضيق من التحقق الكامل من القافية الخليلية، والقبول الآلي لا يثبت الجودة الأدبية. يبقى توليد AI معطّلًا في النسخة العامة.","notebookTitle":"دفتر الهندسة","allNotes":"العودة إلى الملاحظات","noteLabel":"ملاحظة هندسية","readingTime":"3 دقائق للقراءة","articleContext":"شرح للخيارات التقنية والنتائج الموثّقة في مستودع المشروع.","contentsLabel":"في هذه المقالة","sourcesTitle":"المصادر والتنفيذ","sourceReadme":"README المشروع","sourceEvidence":"التقييم والنتائج","exploreProject":"استكشف المشروع","continueReading":"تابع القراءة","writtenBy":"بقلم","evidenceCaption":"استنادًا إلى README المشروع والتقييمات المرتبطة به.","copyLink":"نسخ الرابط","linkCopied":"تم نسخ الرابط","switchDark":"تفعيل المظهر الداكن","switchLight":"تفعيل المظهر الفاتح","opensNewTab":"يفتح في علامة تبويب جديدة","technologyLabel":"التقنيات","contactLinksLabel":"التواصل والحسابات الاجتماعية","homeLabel":"الصفحة الرئيسية لطه الشلي","browseNotebook":"تصفّح دفتر الهندسة","navNotebook":"الدفتر","sectionLink":"رابط هذا القسم","projectSectionsLabel":"أقسام المشروع","projectScreenshots":"الصور","projectArchitecture":"آلية العمل","projectDecisions":"القرارات"},"es":{"languageLabel":"Idioma","navAbout":"Sobre mí","navWork":"Trabajo","navContact":"Contacto","intro":"HOLA, SOY TAHA","heroTitle":"Taha Chelly.<br><span>Ingeniero de software.</span><br>Me mueve crear.","heroDescription":"Desarrollo productos con AI que combinan sistemas fiables con una experiencia de uso sencilla e intuitiva.","connect":"Hablemos","github":"GitHub","currentlyAt":"Actualmente en <a href=\"#work\">SpeakDuo</a>","role":"Ingeniero de software","portraitNote":"Convierto ideas en experiencias reales","aboutKicker":"UN POCO DE CONTEXTO","aboutTitle":"La persona detrás del código.","aboutText":"Soy Taha Chelly, ingeniero de software en Sfax, Túnez. Me gusta acompañar cada etapa de un producto: desde una interfaz clara y un backend fiable hasta la inteligencia que lo hace realmente útil.","aboutDetail":"Soy graduado en ingeniería de software con experiencia en backends Python, API REST y aplicaciones de AI con FastAPI, SQL y Docker. He contribuido a funciones en producción de SpeakDuo y desarrollado proyectos de AI de principio a fin. Busco un puesto de desarrollador Python a tiempo completo para crear servicios backend fiables y crecer en ingeniería de AI.","tagFullStack":"Desarrollo full-stack","tagAI":"Aplicaciones de AI","tagRealtime":"Experiencias en tiempo real","workKicker":"EN QUÉ ESTOY TRABAJANDO","workTitle":"Crear con propósito.","current":"Puesto actual","workHeading":"Ayudo a las personas a aprender idiomas.<br>Una conversación cada vez.","workDescription":"Trabajo en el backend, la aplicación web y los agentes de voz de SpeakDuo: traducción en directo, comentarios sobre el habla, actividades interactivas y práctica personalizada.","remote":"Remoto","toolkitTitle":"Algunas herramientas que uso","contactKicker":"LAS BUENAS IDEAS EMPIEZAN CON UNA CONVERSACIÓN","contactTitle":"Creemos algo<br><span>que merezca la pena compartir.</span>","footerLine":"Hecho con cuidado. En constante evolución.","backToTop":"Volver arriba ↑","navProjects":"Proyectos","projectsKicker":"PROYECTOS SELECCIONADOS","projectsTitle":"Ideas que cobran vida.","viewProject":"Explorar el proyecto ↗","projectCategory":"AUDIO · AI · WEB","projectSummary":"Descubre quién recita y qué aleya estás escuchando. Reconocimiento de recitaciones del Corán, en directo o mediante archivos de audio.","backProjects":"← Todos los proyectos","liveDemo":"Probar la demo","sourceCode":"Ver en GitHub","screenshotsKicker":"EN IMÁGENES","screenshotsTitle":"Dos formas de explorar una recitación.","reciterCaption":"Reconocimiento del recitador: sube audio o escucha en directo.","verseCaption":"Búsqueda de aleyas: encuentra la sura y la aleya recitadas.","approachKicker":"CÓMO FUNCIONA","approachTitle":"Del sonido a la identificación.","reciterTitle":"Identificar al recitador","reciterDetail":"El modelo ECAPA-TDNN genera un voice embedding. ONNX Runtime ejecuta el proceso de inference y la cosine similarity ordena las coincidencias con los perfiles de 20 recitadores.","verseTitle":"Encontrar la aleya","verseDetail":"Un modelo Whisper adaptado al Corán transcribe el audio árabe. El texto normalizado se compara con 6236 aleyas para encontrar las coincidencias probables.","contextTitle":"Escuchar más contexto","contextDetail":"Si la coincidencia es ambigua, la escucha progresiva añade más audio. Los resultados inciertos se indican como tales.","stackKicker":"TECNOLOGÍAS","stackTitle":"La tecnología del proyecto.","frontendDetail":"Frontend: React 19 y TypeScript, con Vite y Tailwind CSS 4. La captura de audio del navegador y la subida de archivos se conectan a la API.","backendDetail":"Backend: Python y FastAPI, con WebSockets para identificar recitadores en directo. ONNX Runtime calcula los speaker embeddings; faster-whisper y CTranslate2 transcriben las recitaciones.","deployDetail":"Despliegue: Docker containers en Render, con Nginx para servir el frontend. GitHub Actions comprueba el backend y el frontend antes de desplegar los servicios modificados.","tryTitle":"Escucha. Descubre.","qafiyaCategory":"IDIOMA · POESÍA · AI","qafiyaSummary":"Un taller de poesía árabe para explorar métrica clásica, rima, escansión y vocalización local.","qafiyaCaptionDesk":"Espacio de escritura — elige un metro clásico y una letra de rima, y después examina el verso.","qafiyaCaptionMobile":"Análisis de poesía árabe adaptado al móvil.","qafiyaApproachTitle":"Del verso escrito a su ritmo.","qafiyaAnalysisTitle":"Analiza los metros clásicos","qafiyaAnalysisDetail":"Comprueba los versos árabes con 16 metros clásicos mediante PyArud. Explora ambos hemistiquios, la escansión binaria, los pies y la letra de rima solicitada (rawi).","qafiyaTashkeelTitle":"Completa la vocalización localmente","qafiyaTashkeelDetail":"Un modelo libtashkeel ONNX incluido de unos 4.8 MB completa los signos vocálicos que faltan en la CPU. Respeta los signos existentes y analiza sin llamar a un LLM.","qafiyaDraftTitle":"La generación es experimental","qafiyaDraftDetail":"Un proveedor opcional redacta poemas y revisa los versos que fallan sin cambiar el texto aceptado. La generación está desactivada en la demo pública.","qafiyaFrontend":"Frontend: React 19, TypeScript y Vite, con una interfaz árabe adaptable de derecha a izquierda.","qafiyaBackend":"Backend: Python 3.12, FastAPI, PyArud, NumPy y ONNX Runtime para CPU. Un único worker comparte una sesión de inference con uso limitado.","qafiyaDeploy":"Alojamiento: frontend en Cloudflare Pages y API Docker en Render. GitHub Actions comprueba el frontend, el backend y el container de producción.","qafiyaTryTitle":"Explora la métrica y la rima.","generationPaused":"El análisis está disponible en la demo. La generación con AI está desactivada.","cvFormat":"PDF · 129 KB","story0Title":"Cuando un fragmento de audio necesita más contexto","story0Summary":"Separar la identificación del recitador de la búsqueda de aleyas e integrar la incertidumbre en la experiencia de escucha.","story0Section0Title":"Dos preguntas, dos pipelines","story0Section0Text":"Reconocer una voz y reconocer palabras son problemas distintos. Quranic Shazam utiliza speaker embeddings ECAPA-TDNN con ONNX Runtime para ordenar las coincidencias con 20 perfiles de recitadores. La búsqueda de aleyas usa un modelo Whisper adaptado al Corán, normaliza la transcripción árabe y la compara con 6.236 aleyas. El modelo de speaker embeddings se utiliza en su estado pretrained, sin fine-tuning con grabaciones del Corán.","story0Section1Title":"Pedir más contexto antes de dar una respuesta segura","story0Section1Text":"Una recitación breve puede coincidir con varias aleyas. La escucha progresiva añade contexto de audio hasta un límite de 60 segundos, y los resultados ambiguos siguen marcados como inciertos. Se acepta una espera mayor a cambio de más contexto, en lugar de forzar una respuesta temprana.","story0Section2Title":"Ejecutar inference fuera del event loop","story0Section2Text":"El proceso de inference del modelo se ejecuta fuera del event loop asíncrono de la API. Los archivos están limitados a 25 MB y cada modo tiene su propio límite de duración. Estas restricciones acotan las solicitudes costosas mientras la API admite archivos y sesiones de micrófono en directo.","story0Section3Title":"Medir una tarea bien definida","story0Section3Text":"La evaluación offline del 5 de septiembre de 2026 obtuvo un 97,31 % en top-1 y un 99,10 % en top-3 para identificar recitadores en 781 fragmentos reservados para evaluación, con suras distintas para crear perfiles y evaluar. Estas cifras describen ese benchmark de recitadores; no miden la identificación de aleyas ni garantizan resultados con cualquier micrófono, ruido o grabación.","story1Title":"Prosodia árabe en un pequeño servidor con CPU","story1Summary":"Un modelo de vocalización de 4.8 MB, respeto por los signos vocálicos existentes y límites claros para el análisis automático.","story1Section0Title":"Ajustar el modelo a los recursos disponibles","story1Section0Text":"Qafiya combina el análisis de prosodia clásica de PyArud con un modelo libtashkeel ONNX incluido de unos 4.8 MB. La vocalización se ejecuta localmente en CPU sin PyTorch, Transformers, GPU ni servidor externo de modelos. Un único Uvicorn worker comparte una sesión de inference acotada y serializada para controlar las copias del modelo y las ejecuciones simultáneas.","story1Section1Title":"Respetar el texto del autor","story1Section1Text":"Los signos vocálicos existentes tienen prioridad. La vocalización automática completa los signos que faltan e informa de los cambios; la interfaz muestra el texto analizado y conserva el original. Esta distinción importa porque la escansión depende de la pronunciación y una vocal predicha puede cambiar el resultado.","story1Section2Title":"Probar el container y explicar los límites","story1Section2Text":"La prueba local documentada ejecutó la imagen de producción con una carga que abarca la aplicación ASGI, bajo límites de 512 MiB de RAM y 0.1 CPU. El process RSS alcanzó 142.55 MiB sin errores out-of-memory. Es evidencia de una carga acotada, no una garantía para cualquier tráfico público. En otra muestra de 12 versos, las coincidencias métricas de textos parcialmente vocalizados mejoraron de 2/12 a 10/12; los textos completamente desprovistos de signos vocálicos solo alcanzaron 2/12.","story1Section3Title":"Acotar las revisiones y conservar el texto válido","story1Section3Text":"El workflow experimental comprueba la métrica y el rawi solicitado, y revisa los versos que fallan mediante un bucle limitado. El backend conserva los versos aceptados y los hemistiquios válidos. La igualdad del rawi no equivale a validar toda la rima clásica, y la aceptación automática no certifica calidad literaria. La generación con AI sigue desactivada en la demo pública.","notebookTitle":"Cuaderno de ingeniería","readNote":"Leer la nota técnica","allNotes":"Volver a las notas","noteLabel":"Nota técnica","readingTime":"3 min de lectura","articleContext":"Un recorrido por las decisiones técnicas y los resultados documentados en el repositorio del proyecto.","contentsLabel":"En este artículo","sourcesTitle":"Fuentes e implementación","sourceReadme":"README del proyecto","sourceEvidence":"Evaluación y resultados","exploreProject":"Explorar el proyecto","continueReading":"Seguir leyendo","writtenBy":"Por","writingTitle":"Las decisiones técnicas, explicadas.","evidenceCaption":"Basado en el README del proyecto y las evaluaciones enlazadas.","copyLink":"Copiar enlace","linkCopied":"Enlace copiado","writingKicker":"Cuaderno de ingeniería","downloadCV":"Descargar CV","contactIntent":"Busco un puesto de desarrollador Python a tiempo completo para crear servicios backend fiables y aplicaciones de AI. Si encaja con tu equipo, hablemos.","employmentDates":"Ingeniero de software · Jul. 2026 — Actualidad","internshipDates":"Anteriormente: prácticas de fin de carrera en SpeakDuo · Ene. — Jul. 2026.","achievementFeedback":"Desarrollé feedback multilingüe de gramática y pronunciación, generación de lecciones y práctica personalizada para la plataforma en producción.","achievementPractice":"Creé el seguimiento de vocabulario, ejercicios de spaced repetition y evaluación CEFR basada en Elo para apoyar el aprendizaje adaptativo.","achievementVoice":"Implementé un voice agent de entrevistas multilingües con LiveKit y optimicé speech recognition para subtítulos en tiempo real mediante voice activity detection.","achievementMultiplayer":"Entregué AI chat, práctica personal de gramática y actividades multiplayer sincronizadas, tanto en el backend como en la aplicación web.","decisionsKicker":"RETOS Y DECISIONES","decisionsTitle":"Por qué funciona así.","switchDark":"Activar el tema oscuro","switchLight":"Activar el tema claro","opensNewTab":"Se abre en una pestaña nueva","technologyLabel":"Tecnologías","contactLinksLabel":"Contacto y redes sociales","homeLabel":"Inicio de Taha Chelly","browseNotebook":"Explorar el cuaderno","navNotebook":"Cuaderno","sectionLink":"Enlace a esta sección","projectSectionsLabel":"Secciones del proyecto","projectScreenshots":"Capturas","projectArchitecture":"Cómo funciona","projectDecisions":"Decisiones"},"de":{"languageLabel":"Sprache","navAbout":"Über mich","navWork":"Arbeit","navContact":"Kontakt","intro":"HALLO, ICH BIN TAHA","heroTitle":"Taha Chelly.<br><span>Softwareentwickler.</span><br>Mit Freude am Gestalten.","heroDescription":"Ich entwickle durchdachte AI-Produkte mit zuverlässigen Systemen und einer intuitiven Benutzeroberfläche.","connect":"Lass uns sprechen","github":"GitHub","currentlyAt":"Derzeit bei <a href=\"#work\">SpeakDuo</a>","role":"Softwareentwickler","portraitNote":"Ich mache aus Ideen echte Erlebnisse","aboutKicker":"KURZ ZU MIR","aboutTitle":"Der Mensch hinter dem Code.","aboutText":"Ich bin Taha Chelly, Softwareentwickler aus Sfax in Tunesien. Mir gefällt der gesamte Weg von der ersten Idee bis zum fertigen Produkt: eine klare Oberfläche, ein zuverlässiges Backend und die passende Intelligenz, die es nützlich macht.","aboutDetail":"Ich bin Absolvent der Softwaretechnik mit Erfahrung in Python-Backends, REST-APIs und AI-Anwendungen mit FastAPI, SQL und Docker. Bei SpeakDuo habe ich an produktiv eingesetzten Funktionen mitgewirkt und eigene AI-Projekte von Anfang bis Ende umgesetzt. Ich suche eine Vollzeitstelle als Python-Entwickler, um zuverlässige Backend-Dienste zu entwickeln und mich im AI-Engineering weiterzuentwickeln.","tagFullStack":"Full-Stack-Entwicklung","tagAI":"AI-Anwendungen","tagRealtime":"Echtzeiterlebnisse","workKicker":"WORAN ICH ARBEITE","workTitle":"Produkte mit Mehrwert entwickeln.","current":"Aktuell","workHeading":"Ich helfe Menschen, Sprachen zu lernen.<br>Gespräch für Gespräch.","workDescription":"Ich arbeite am Backend, an der Web-App und an Sprachagenten von SpeakDuo: Live-Übersetzung, Sprachfeedback, interaktive Aktivitäten und individuelles Üben.","remote":"Remote","toolkitTitle":"Einige Tools, mit denen ich arbeite","contactKicker":"GUTE IDEEN BEGINNEN MIT EINEM GESPRÄCH","contactTitle":"Lass uns etwas schaffen,<br><span>über das man gern spricht.</span>","footerLine":"Mit Sorgfalt entwickelt. Immer im Wandel.","backToTop":"Nach oben ↑","navProjects":"Projekte","projectsKicker":"AUSGEWÄHLTE PROJEKTE","projectsTitle":"Ideen werden Wirklichkeit.","viewProject":"Projekt entdecken ↗","projectCategory":"AUDIO · AI · WEB","projectSummary":"Erkenne den Rezitator und finde den Vers, den du hörst. Eine App zur Erkennung von Koranrezitationen mit Live-Aufnahme und Audio-Upload.","backProjects":"← Alle Projekte","liveDemo":"Live-Demo ausprobieren","sourceCode":"Auf GitHub ansehen","screenshotsKicker":"EINBLICKE","screenshotsTitle":"Zwei Wege, eine Rezitation zu entdecken.","reciterCaption":"Rezitator erkennen: Audiodatei hochladen oder live zuhören.","verseCaption":"Verse finden: Sure und Vers einer Rezitation bestimmen.","approachKicker":"SO FUNKTIONIERT ES","approachTitle":"Vom Klang zum passenden Treffer.","reciterTitle":"Rezitator erkennen","reciterDetail":"Das ECAPA-TDNN-Modell erzeugt ein Voice Embedding. ONNX Runtime führt die Inference aus; anschließend ordnet Cosine Similarity die Treffer anhand der Profile von 20 Rezitatoren.","verseTitle":"Vers finden","verseDetail":"Ein auf den Koran abgestimmtes Whisper-Modell transkribiert arabische Aufnahmen. Der normalisierte Text wird mit 6.236 Versen verglichen.","contextTitle":"Mehr Kontext hören","contextDetail":"Bei mehrdeutigen Versen sammelt die schrittweise Aufnahme mehr Kontext. Unsichere Ergebnisse bleiben entsprechend gekennzeichnet.","stackKicker":"TECHNOLOGIEN","stackTitle":"Die Technik dahinter.","frontendDetail":"Frontend: React 19, TypeScript, Vite und Tailwind CSS 4. Browsermikrofon und Audio-Uploads sind mit der API verbunden.","backendDetail":"Backend: Python und FastAPI mit WebSockets zur Live-Erkennung von Rezitatoren. ONNX Runtime berechnet Speaker Embeddings; faster-whisper und CTranslate2 transkribieren die Rezitationen.","deployDetail":"Bereitstellung: Docker-Container auf Render, mit Nginx für das Frontend. GitHub Actions prüft Backend und Frontend, bevor geänderte Dienste bereitgestellt werden.","tryTitle":"Hören. Entdecken.","qafiyaCategory":"SPRACHE · POESIE · AI","qafiyaSummary":"Eine Werkstatt für arabische Poesie mit klassischem Versmaß, Reim, Skansion und lokaler Vokalisierung.","qafiyaCaptionDesk":"Schreibbereich — klassisches Versmaß und Reimbuchstaben wählen und anschließend den Vers untersuchen.","qafiyaCaptionMobile":"Arabische Versanalyse im mobilfreundlichen Layout.","qafiyaApproachTitle":"Vom geschriebenen Vers zu seinem Rhythmus.","qafiyaAnalysisTitle":"Klassisches Versmaß analysieren","qafiyaAnalysisDetail":"Prüfe arabische Verse mit PyArud anhand von 16 klassischen Metren. Untersuche beide Halbverse, die binäre Skansion, die Versfüße und den gewünschten Reimbuchstaben (rawi).","qafiyaTashkeelTitle":"Vokalisierung lokal ergänzen","qafiyaTashkeelDetail":"Ein mitgeliefertes libtashkeel-ONNX-Modell von etwa 4.8 MB ergänzt fehlende Vokalzeichen auf der CPU. Vorhandene Zeichen bleiben maßgeblich; die Analyse ruft kein LLM auf.","qafiyaDraftTitle":"Gedichtentwürfe sind experimentell","qafiyaDraftDetail":"Ein optionaler Anbieter entwirft Gedichte und überarbeitet fehlerhafte Verse, ohne akzeptierten Text zu ändern. In der öffentlichen Demo ist die Generierung deaktiviert.","qafiyaFrontend":"Frontend: React 19, TypeScript und Vite mit responsivem arabischem RTL-Layout.","qafiyaBackend":"Backend: Python 3.12, FastAPI, PyArud, NumPy und ONNX Runtime auf der CPU. Ein Worker nutzt eine gemeinsame, begrenzte Inference Session.","qafiyaDeploy":"Hosting: Frontend auf Cloudflare Pages und Docker-API auf Render. GitHub Actions prüft Frontend, Backend und Production Container.","qafiyaTryTitle":"Versmaß und Reim entdecken.","generationPaused":"Die Analyse ist in der Demo verfügbar. AI-Generierung ist deaktiviert.","cvFormat":"PDF · 129 KB","story0Title":"Wenn ein Audioausschnitt mehr Kontext braucht","story0Summary":"Sprechererkennung und Verssuche trennen und Unsicherheit im Ablauf sichtbar machen.","story0Section0Title":"Zwei Fragen, zwei Pipelines","story0Section0Text":"Eine Stimme zu erkennen und Wörter zu erkennen sind unterschiedliche Aufgaben. Quranic Shazam verwendet ECAPA-TDNN Speaker Embeddings mit ONNX Runtime, um Treffer anhand von 20 Rezitatorenprofilen zu ordnen. Die Verssuche nutzt dagegen ein an den Koran angepasstes Whisper-Modell, normalisiert das arabische Transkript und vergleicht es mit 6.236 Versen. Das Modell für Speaker Embeddings wird im Pretrained-Zustand verwendet; ein Fine-Tuning mit Koranaufnahmen fand nicht statt.","story0Section1Title":"Vor einer sicheren Antwort mehr Kontext sammeln","story0Section1Text":"Eine kurze Rezitation kann zu mehreren Versen passen. Die schrittweise Aufnahme ergänzt Audiokontext bis zu einer Grenze von 60 Sekunden. Mehrdeutige Ergebnisse bleiben als unsicher gekennzeichnet. Dafür wird eine längere Aufnahmezeit in Kauf genommen, statt frühzeitig eine Antwort zu erzwingen.","story0Section2Title":"Inference außerhalb des Event Loop ausführen","story0Section2Text":"Die Inference des Modells läuft außerhalb des asynchronen Event Loop der API. Dateien sind auf 25 MB begrenzt; je nach Erkennungsmodus gelten zusätzliche Grenzen für die Audiodauer. So bleiben aufwendige Anfragen begrenzt, während die API sowohl Dateien als auch Live-Mikrofonsitzungen unterstützt.","story0Section3Title":"Eine klar definierte Aufgabe messen","story0Section3Text":"Die Offline-Auswertung vom 5. September 2026 ergab 97,31 % Top-1 und 99,10 % Top-3 bei der Rezitatorenerkennung auf 781 zurückgehaltenen Clips. Für Profile und Auswertung wurden unterschiedliche Suren verwendet. Diese Werte beschreiben nur diesen Rezitatoren-Benchmark. Sie messen keine Verserkennung und garantieren keine Ergebnisse bei beliebigen Mikrofonen, Störgeräuschen oder Aufnahmen.","story1Title":"Arabische Verslehre auf einem kleinen CPU-Server","story1Summary":"Ein 4.8-MB-Modell zur Vokalisierung, unveränderte vorhandene Vokalzeichen und klare Grenzen der automatischen Analyse.","story1Section0Title":"Das Modell an die verfügbaren Ressourcen anpassen","story1Section0Text":"Qafiya verbindet die klassische Versanalyse von PyArud mit einem mitgelieferten libtashkeel-ONNX-Modell von etwa 4.8 MB. Die Vokalisierung läuft lokal auf der CPU, ohne PyTorch, Transformers, GPU oder externen Modellserver. Ein einzelner Uvicorn Worker nutzt eine gemeinsame, begrenzte und serialisierte Inference Session. So bleiben Modellkopien und parallele Ausführungen kontrollierbar.","story1Section1Title":"Den Text des Autors bewahren","story1Section1Text":"Vorhandene Vokalzeichen haben Vorrang. Die automatische Vokalisierung ergänzt fehlende Zeichen und legt Änderungen offen. Die Oberfläche zeigt den analysierten Text und bewahrt zugleich die ursprüngliche Eingabe. Das ist wichtig, weil die Skansion von der Aussprache abhängt und ein vorhergesagter Vokal das Ergebnis verändern kann.","story1Section2Title":"Den Container testen und Grenzen benennen","story1Section2Text":"Der dokumentierte lokale Test führte das Production Image mit einer Last über die gesamte ASGI-Anwendung unter 512 MiB RAM und 0.1 CPU aus. Der Process RSS erreichte maximal 142.55 MiB, ohne Out-of-Memory-Fehler. Das belegt das Verhalten bei einer begrenzten Last und garantiert keine Stabilität bei beliebigem öffentlichem Traffic. In einer separaten Stichprobe mit 12 Versen stiegen die Metrumtreffer bei teilweise vokalisierten Texten von 2/12 auf 10/12; Texte ganz ohne Vokalzeichen erreichten nur 2/12.","story1Section3Title":"Korrekturen begrenzen und gültigen Text erhalten","story1Section3Text":"Der experimentelle Workflow prüft Metrum und gewünschten Rawi und überarbeitet fehlerhafte Verse in einer begrenzten Schleife. Das Backend erhält akzeptierte Verse und gültige Halbverse. Die Gleichheit des Rawi ist keine vollständige Prüfung des klassischen Reims, und maschinelle Akzeptanz bestätigt keine literarische Qualität. Die AI-Generierung bleibt in der öffentlichen Demo deaktiviert.","notebookTitle":"Engineering-Notizbuch","readNote":"Technische Notiz lesen","allNotes":"Zurück zu allen Notizen","noteLabel":"Technische Notiz","readingTime":"3 Min. Lesezeit","articleContext":"Ein Einblick in die technischen Entscheidungen und dokumentierten Ergebnisse im Repository des Projekts.","contentsLabel":"In diesem Artikel","sourcesTitle":"Quellen und Implementierung","sourceReadme":"Projekt-README","sourceEvidence":"Auswertung und Nachweise","exploreProject":"Projekt ansehen","continueReading":"Weiterlesen","writtenBy":"Von","writingTitle":"Technische Entscheidungen verständlich erklärt.","evidenceCaption":"Basierend auf dem Projekt-README und den verlinkten Auswertungen.","copyLink":"Link kopieren","linkCopied":"Link kopiert","writingKicker":"Engineering-Notizbuch","downloadCV":"Lebenslauf herunterladen","contactIntent":"Ich suche eine Vollzeitstelle als Python-Entwickler, um zuverlässige Backend-Dienste und AI-Anwendungen zu entwickeln. Wenn das zu eurem Team passt, freue ich mich auf ein Gespräch.","employmentDates":"Softwareentwickler · Juli 2026 — Heute","internshipDates":"Zuvor: Abschlusspraktikum bei SpeakDuo · Jan. — Juli 2026.","achievementFeedback":"Ich habe mehrsprachiges Feedback zu Grammatik und Aussprache, die Generierung von Lektionen und personalisierte Übungen für die produktiv eingesetzte Plattform entwickelt.","achievementPractice":"Ich habe die Erfassung des Wortschatzes, Übungen mit Spaced Repetition und eine Elo-basierte CEFR-Bewertung für adaptives Lernen umgesetzt.","achievementVoice":"Ich habe mit LiveKit einen mehrsprachigen Voice Agent für Interviews entwickelt und die Speech Recognition für Echtzeituntertitel mithilfe von Voice Activity Detection optimiert.","achievementMultiplayer":"Ich habe AI Chat, persönliches Grammatiktraining und synchronisierte Multiplayer-Lernaktivitäten im Backend und in der Web-App umgesetzt.","decisionsKicker":"HERAUSFORDERUNGEN UND ABWÄGUNGEN","decisionsTitle":"Die Gründe für diese technischen Entscheidungen.","switchDark":"Dunkles Design aktivieren","switchLight":"Helles Design aktivieren","opensNewTab":"Öffnet in einem neuen Tab","technologyLabel":"Technologien","contactLinksLabel":"Kontakt und soziale Profile","homeLabel":"Startseite von Taha Chelly","browseNotebook":"Notizbuch ansehen","navNotebook":"Notizbuch","sectionLink":"Link zu diesem Abschnitt","projectSectionsLabel":"Projektabschnitte","projectScreenshots":"Screenshots","projectArchitecture":"Funktionsweise","projectDecisions":"Entscheidungen"},"fr":{"languageLabel":"Langue","navAbout":"À propos","navWork":"Travail","navContact":"Contact","intro":"BONJOUR, JE SUIS TAHA","heroTitle":"Taha Chelly.<br><span>Ingénieur logiciel.</span><br>J’aime créer.","heroDescription":"Je développe des produits intégrant des fonctionnalités AI, en associant des systèmes fiables à une expérience simple et intuitive.","connect":"Parlons-en","github":"GitHub","currentlyAt":"Actuellement chez <a href=\"#work\">SpeakDuo</a>","role":"Ingénieur logiciel","portraitNote":"Je transforme les idées en expériences concrètes","aboutKicker":"QUELQUES MOTS","aboutTitle":"La personne derrière le code.","aboutText":"Je suis Taha Chelly, ingénieur logiciel à Sfax, en Tunisie. J’aime accompagner un produit de l’idée à sa réalisation : une interface claire, un backend fiable et l’intelligence qui le rend vraiment utile.","aboutDetail":"Diplômé en génie logiciel, j’ai de l’expérience dans le développement de backends Python, d’API REST et d’applications AI avec FastAPI, SQL et Docker. J’ai contribué à des fonctionnalités en production chez SpeakDuo et réalisé des projets AI de bout en bout. Je recherche un poste de développeur Python à temps plein pour construire des services backend fiables et approfondir mon expertise en AI engineering.","tagFullStack":"Développement full-stack","tagAI":"Applications AI","tagRealtime":"Expériences en temps réel","workKicker":"MON TRAVAIL ACTUEL","workTitle":"Créer avec du sens.","current":"Poste actuel","workHeading":"J’aide chacun à apprendre des langues.<br>Une conversation à la fois.","workDescription":"Je travaille sur le backend, l’application web et les agents vocaux de SpeakDuo : traduction en direct, retours sur la parole, activités interactives et pratique personnalisée.","remote":"À distance","toolkitTitle":"Quelques outils que j’utilise","contactKicker":"LES BELLES IDÉES COMMENCENT PAR UNE CONVERSATION","contactTitle":"Créons quelque chose<br><span>qui mérite qu’on en parle.</span>","footerLine":"Créé avec soin. Toujours en évolution.","backToTop":"Retour en haut ↑","navProjects":"Projets","projectsKicker":"PROJETS SÉLECTIONNÉS","projectsTitle":"Des idées qui prennent vie.","viewProject":"Découvrir le projet ↗","projectCategory":"AUDIO · AI · WEB","projectSummary":"Identifiez le récitateur et retrouvez le verset que vous écoutez. Une application de reconnaissance de récitations du Coran, en direct ou à partir d’un fichier audio.","backProjects":"← Tous les projets","liveDemo":"Essayer la démo","sourceCode":"Voir sur GitHub","screenshotsKicker":"EN IMAGES","screenshotsTitle":"Deux façons d’explorer une récitation.","reciterCaption":"Reconnaissance du récitateur : importez un fichier ou écoutez en direct.","verseCaption":"Recherche de versets : retrouvez la sourate et le verset récités.","approachKicker":"COMMENT ÇA MARCHE","approachTitle":"Du son à la reconnaissance.","reciterTitle":"Identifier le récitateur","reciterDetail":"Le modèle ECAPA-TDNN génère un voice embedding. ONNX Runtime exécute le traitement d’inference, puis la cosine similarity permet de classer les correspondances avec les profils de 20 récitateurs.","verseTitle":"Retrouver le verset","verseDetail":"Un modèle Whisper adapté au Coran transcrit l’audio arabe. Le texte normalisé est comparé à 6 236 versets pour retrouver la sourate et les versets probables.","contextTitle":"Écouter davantage","contextDetail":"Si plusieurs versets restent possibles, l’écoute progressive recueille plus de contexte. Les résultats incertains sont signalés comme tels.","stackKicker":"TECHNOLOGIES","stackTitle":"Les outils derrière le projet.","frontendDetail":"Frontend : React 19 et TypeScript, avec Vite et Tailwind CSS 4. La capture audio du navigateur et l’envoi de fichiers se connectent à l’API.","backendDetail":"Backend : Python et FastAPI, avec WebSockets pour identifier les récitateurs en direct. ONNX Runtime calcule les speaker embeddings ; faster-whisper et CTranslate2 transcrivent les récitations.","deployDetail":"Déploiement : Docker containers sur Render, avec Nginx pour servir le frontend. GitHub Actions vérifie le backend et le frontend avant de déployer les services modifiés.","tryTitle":"Écoutez. Découvrez.","qafiyaCategory":"LANGUE · POÉSIE · AI","qafiyaSummary":"Un atelier de poésie arabe pour explorer le mètre classique, la rime, la scansion et la vocalisation locale.","qafiyaCaptionDesk":"Espace d’écriture — choisissez un mètre classique et une lettre de rime, puis examinez le vers.","qafiyaCaptionMobile":"Analyse de poésie arabe adaptée au mobile.","qafiyaApproachTitle":"Du vers écrit à son rythme.","qafiyaAnalysisTitle":"Analyser le mètre classique","qafiyaAnalysisDetail":"Comparez les vers arabes à 16 mètres classiques avec PyArud. Explorez les deux hémistiches, la scansion binaire, les pieds et la lettre de rime demandée (rawi).","qafiyaTashkeelTitle":"Compléter les signes vocaliques localement","qafiyaTashkeelDetail":"Un modèle libtashkeel ONNX embarqué d’environ 4.8 MB complète les signes vocaliques manquants sur CPU. Les signes déjà fournis restent prioritaires ; l’analyse n’appelle pas de LLM.","qafiyaDraftTitle":"La génération reste expérimentale","qafiyaDraftDetail":"Un adaptateur optionnel rédige des poèmes et corrige les vers en échec tout en préservant le texte accepté. La génération est désactivée sur la démo publique.","qafiyaFrontend":"Frontend : React 19, TypeScript et Vite, avec une interface arabe RTL adaptative.","qafiyaBackend":"Backend : Python 3.12, FastAPI, PyArud, NumPy et ONNX Runtime sur CPU. Un seul worker partage une session d’inference dont l’utilisation est limitée.","qafiyaDeploy":"Hébergement : frontend sur Cloudflare Pages et API Docker sur Render. GitHub Actions vérifie le frontend, le backend et le container de production.","qafiyaTryTitle":"Explorez le mètre et la rime.","generationPaused":"L’analyse est disponible sur la démo. La génération AI est désactivée.","downloadCV":"Télécharger le CV","contactIntent":"Je recherche un poste de développeur Python à temps plein pour construire des services backend fiables et des applications AI. Si ce profil correspond aux besoins de votre équipe, parlons-en.","employmentDates":"Ingénieur logiciel · Juil. 2026 — Aujourd’hui","internshipDates":"Auparavant : stage de fin d’études chez SpeakDuo · Janv. — Juil. 2026.","achievementFeedback":"J’ai développé des retours multilingues sur la grammaire et la prononciation, la génération de leçons et des exercices personnalisés pour la plateforme en production.","achievementPractice":"J’ai créé le suivi du vocabulaire, des exercices de spaced repetition et une évaluation CEFR fondée sur Elo pour soutenir l’apprentissage adaptatif.","achievementVoice":"J’ai développé un agent d’entretien vocal multilingue avec LiveKit et optimisé la speech recognition pour les sous-titres en direct à l’aide de la voice activity detection.","achievementMultiplayer":"J’ai réalisé des fonctionnalités de AI chat, des exercices de grammaire personnalisés et des activités d’apprentissage multiplayer synchronisées, du backend à l’application web.","writingKicker":"Carnet d’ingénierie","writingTitle":"Les choix techniques, expliqués.","decisionsKicker":"DÉFIS ET COMPROMIS","decisionsTitle":"Les raisons de ces choix techniques.","readNote":"Lire la note technique","cvFormat":"PDF · 129 KB","story0Title":"Quand un extrait audio ne suffit pas","story0Summary":"Distinguer l’identification d’une voix de celle d’un verset, et intégrer l’incertitude au parcours d’écoute.","story0Section0Title":"Deux questions, deux pipelines","story0Section0Text":"Reconnaître une voix et reconnaître des mots sont deux problèmes différents. Quranic Shazam utilise des speaker embeddings ECAPA-TDNN avec ONNX Runtime pour classer les correspondances avec 20 profils de récitateurs. Pour retrouver un verset, un modèle Whisper adapté au Coran transcrit l’audio, puis le texte arabe est normalisé et comparé à 6 236 versets. Le modèle de speaker embeddings est utilisé tel quel (pretrained), sans fine-tuning sur des récitations du Coran.","story0Section1Title":"Demander du contexte avant de conclure","story0Section1Text":"Un court extrait peut correspondre à plusieurs versets. L’écoute progressive ajoute du contexte audio, jusqu’à 60 secondes, et les résultats ambigus restent signalés comme incertains. Ce choix privilégie une écoute plus longue pour recueillir davantage de contexte, plutôt qu’une réponse prématurée.","story0Section2Title":"Garder l’inference hors de l’event loop","story0Section2Text":"L’inference du modèle s’exécute en dehors de l’event loop asynchrone de l’API. Les fichiers sont limités à 25 MB, avec des durées audio maximales propres à chaque mode. Ces limites bornent le coût des requêtes tout en permettant l’envoi de fichiers et l’écoute au microphone en direct.","story0Section3Title":"Mesurer une tâche bien définie","story0Section3Text":"L’évaluation offline du 5 septembre 2026 rapporte 97,31 % en top-1 et 99,10 % en top-3 sur 781 extraits réservés à l’évaluation, avec des sourates distinctes pour les profils et les tests. Ces chiffres concernent uniquement ce benchmark d’identification des récitateurs. Ils ne mesurent pas la reconnaissance des versets et ne garantissent pas les résultats avec n’importe quel microphone, bruit ambiant ou enregistrement.","story1Title":"La prosodie arabe sur un petit serveur CPU","story1Summary":"Un modèle de vocalisation de 4.8 MB, des signes vocaliques préservés et des limites explicites pour l’analyse automatique.","story1Section0Title":"Adapter le modèle aux ressources disponibles","story1Section0Text":"Qafiya associe l’analyse de la prosodie classique de PyArud à un modèle libtashkeel ONNX embarqué d’environ 4.8 MB. La vocalisation s’exécute localement sur CPU, sans PyTorch, Transformers, GPU ni serveur de modèles externe. Un seul Uvicorn worker partage une session d’inference dont les requêtes sont limitées et exécutées en série, afin de maîtriser le nombre de copies du modèle et les exécutions simultanées.","story1Section1Title":"Respecter le texte de l’auteur","story1Section1Text":"Les signes vocaliques déjà présents restent prioritaires. La vocalisation automatique complète les signes manquants et indique les modifications ; l’interface affiche le texte analysé tout en conservant l’original. Cette distinction compte, car la scansion dépend de la prononciation : une voyelle prédite peut changer le résultat.","story1Section2Title":"Tester le container et préciser les limites","story1Section2Text":"Le test local documenté a exécuté l’image de production sur l’ensemble de l’application ASGI, avec des plafonds de 512 MiB de RAM et 0.1 CPU. Le process RSS a atteint 142.55 MiB sans erreur out-of-memory. Cette mesure porte sur une charge limitée et ne garantit pas le comportement sous un trafic public quelconque. Sur un autre échantillon de 12 vers, les correspondances de mètre sont passées de 2/12 à 10/12 à partir de textes partiellement vocalisés ; les textes entièrement dépourvus de signes vocaliques n’ont atteint que 2/12.","story1Section3Title":"Limiter les corrections et préserver le texte valide","story1Section3Text":"Le workflow expérimental vérifie le mètre et le rawi demandé, puis corrige les vers qui ne respectent pas ces contraintes dans une boucle limitée. Le backend conserve les vers acceptés et les hémistiches valides. L’égalité du rawi ne suffit pas à valider toute la rime classique, et l’acceptation automatique ne certifie pas la qualité littéraire. La génération par AI reste désactivée sur la démo publique.","notebookTitle":"Carnet d’ingénierie","allNotes":"Retour aux notes","noteLabel":"Note technique","readingTime":"3 min de lecture","articleContext":"Une présentation des choix techniques et des résultats documentés dans le dépôt du projet.","contentsLabel":"Dans cet article","sourcesTitle":"Sources et implémentation","sourceReadme":"README du projet","sourceEvidence":"Évaluation et résultats","exploreProject":"Explorer le projet","continueReading":"Poursuivre la lecture","writtenBy":"Par","evidenceCaption":"D’après le README du projet et les évaluations associées.","copyLink":"Copier le lien","linkCopied":"Lien copié","switchDark":"Passer au thème sombre","switchLight":"Passer au thème clair","opensNewTab":"S’ouvre dans un nouvel onglet","technologyLabel":"Technologies","contactLinksLabel":"Contact et réseaux sociaux","homeLabel":"Accueil de Taha Chelly","browseNotebook":"Parcourir le carnet","navNotebook":"Carnet","sectionLink":"Lien vers cette section","projectSectionsLabel":"Rubriques du projet","projectScreenshots":"Captures","projectArchitecture":"Fonctionnement","projectDecisions":"Choix techniques"},"it":{"languageLabel":"Lingua","navAbout":"Chi sono","navWork":"Lavoro","navContact":"Contatti","intro":"CIAO, SONO TAHA","heroTitle":"Taha Chelly.<br><span>Ingegnere del software.</span><br>Mi piace creare.","heroDescription":"Sviluppo prodotti con AI che uniscono sistemi affidabili a un’esperienza d’uso semplice e intuitiva.","connect":"Parliamone","github":"GitHub","currentlyAt":"Attualmente in <a href=\"#work\">SpeakDuo</a>","role":"Ingegnere del software","portraitNote":"Trasformo le idee in esperienze concrete","aboutKicker":"QUALCHE INFORMAZIONE","aboutTitle":"La persona dietro il codice.","aboutText":"Sono Taha Chelly, ingegnere del software a Sfax, in Tunisia. Mi piace seguire un prodotto dall’idea alla realizzazione: un’interfaccia chiara, un backend affidabile e l’intelligenza che lo rende davvero utile.","aboutDetail":"Sono laureato in ingegneria del software con esperienza nello sviluppo di backend Python, API REST e applicazioni di AI con FastAPI, SQL e Docker. Ho contribuito a funzionalità in produzione di SpeakDuo e realizzato progetti di AI completi. Cerco un ruolo a tempo pieno come sviluppatore Python per creare servizi backend affidabili e crescere nell’ingegneria dell’AI.","tagFullStack":"Sviluppo full-stack","tagAI":"Applicazioni AI","tagRealtime":"Esperienze in tempo reale","workKicker":"A COSA STO LAVORANDO","workTitle":"Costruire con uno scopo.","current":"Ruolo attuale","workHeading":"Aiuto le persone a imparare le lingue.<br>Una conversazione alla volta.","workDescription":"Lavoro sul backend, sull’app web e sugli agenti vocali di SpeakDuo: traduzione dal vivo, feedback sul parlato, attività interattive ed esercizi personalizzati.","remote":"Da remoto","toolkitTitle":"Alcuni strumenti che uso","contactKicker":"LE BELLE IDEE INIZIANO CON UNA CONVERSAZIONE","contactTitle":"Creiamo qualcosa<br><span>di cui valga la pena parlare.</span>","footerLine":"Creato con cura. In continua evoluzione.","backToTop":"Torna all’inizio ↑","navProjects":"Progetti","projectsKicker":"PROGETTI SELEZIONATI","projectsTitle":"Idee che prendono vita.","viewProject":"Esplora il progetto ↗","projectCategory":"AUDIO · AI · WEB","projectSummary":"Scopri chi recita e quale versetto stai ascoltando. Un’app per riconoscere le recitazioni del Corano, dal vivo o caricando un file audio.","backProjects":"← Tutti i progetti","liveDemo":"Prova la demo","sourceCode":"Vedi su GitHub","screenshotsKicker":"UNO SGUARDO ALL’APP","screenshotsTitle":"Due modi per esplorare una recitazione.","reciterCaption":"Riconoscimento del recitatore: carica un audio o ascolta dal vivo.","verseCaption":"Ricerca dei versetti: trova la sura e il versetto recitati.","approachKicker":"COME FUNZIONA","approachTitle":"Dal suono al riconoscimento.","reciterTitle":"Riconoscere il recitatore","reciterDetail":"Il modello ECAPA-TDNN genera un voice embedding. ONNX Runtime esegue la fase di inference; la cosine similarity ordina poi le corrispondenze con i profili di 20 recitatori.","verseTitle":"Trovare il versetto","verseDetail":"Un modello Whisper adattato al Corano trascrive l’audio arabo. Il testo normalizzato viene confrontato con 6236 versetti.","contextTitle":"Ascoltare più contesto","contextDetail":"Se il versetto è ambiguo, l’ascolto progressivo raccoglie più audio. I risultati incerti rimangono segnalati come tali.","stackKicker":"TECNOLOGIE","stackTitle":"La tecnologia del progetto.","frontendDetail":"Frontend: React 19, TypeScript, Vite e Tailwind CSS 4. Microfono del browser e file audio si collegano all’API.","backendDetail":"Backend: Python e FastAPI, con WebSockets per identificare i recitatori in diretta. ONNX Runtime calcola gli speaker embeddings; faster-whisper e CTranslate2 trascrivono le recitazioni.","deployDetail":"Deploy: Docker containers su Render, con Nginx per servire il frontend. GitHub Actions verifica backend e frontend prima del deploy dei servizi modificati.","tryTitle":"Ascolta. Scopri.","qafiyaCategory":"LINGUA · POESIA · AI","qafiyaSummary":"Un laboratorio di poesia araba con metro classico, rima, scansione e vocalizzazione locale.","qafiyaCaptionDesk":"Spazio di scrittura — scegli un metro classico e una lettera di rima, poi esamina il verso.","qafiyaCaptionMobile":"Analisi di poesia araba in un layout adatto al telefono.","qafiyaApproachTitle":"Dal verso scritto al suo ritmo.","qafiyaAnalysisTitle":"Analizza il metro classico","qafiyaAnalysisDetail":"Verifica i versi arabi rispetto a 16 metri classici con PyArud. Esplora entrambi gli emistichi, la scansione binaria, i piedi e la lettera di rima richiesta (rawi).","qafiyaTashkeelTitle":"Completa la vocalizzazione in locale","qafiyaTashkeelDetail":"Un modello libtashkeel ONNX incluso di circa 4.8 MB completa i segni vocalici mancanti sulla CPU. Rispetta i segni già presenti e non usa un LLM per l’analisi.","qafiyaDraftTitle":"La generazione è sperimentale","qafiyaDraftDetail":"Un provider opzionale crea bozze e rivede i versi non validi preservando il testo accettato. La generazione è disattivata nella demo pubblica.","qafiyaFrontend":"Frontend: React 19, TypeScript e Vite con interfaccia araba responsive da destra a sinistra.","qafiyaBackend":"Backend: Python 3.12, FastAPI, PyArud, NumPy e ONNX Runtime su CPU. Un singolo worker condivide una sessione di inference il cui utilizzo è limitato.","qafiyaDeploy":"Hosting: frontend su Cloudflare Pages e API Docker su Render. GitHub Actions verifica frontend, backend e container di produzione.","qafiyaTryTitle":"Esplora metro e rima.","generationPaused":"L’analisi è disponibile nella demo. La generazione AI è disattivata.","cvFormat":"PDF · 129 KB","story0Title":"Quando un frammento audio richiede più contesto","story0Summary":"Separare il riconoscimento della voce dalla ricerca del versetto e rendere visibile l’incertezza durante l’ascolto.","story0Section0Title":"Due domande, due pipeline","story0Section0Text":"Riconoscere una voce e riconoscere le parole sono problemi diversi. Quranic Shazam usa speaker embeddings ECAPA-TDNN con ONNX Runtime per ordinare le corrispondenze con 20 profili di recitatori. La ricerca del versetto usa invece un modello Whisper adattato al Corano, normalizza la trascrizione araba e la confronta con 6.236 versetti. Il modello per speaker embeddings viene utilizzato nello stato pretrained, senza fine-tuning su registrazioni coraniche.","story0Section1Title":"Chiedere più contesto prima di dare una risposta certa","story0Section1Text":"Una recitazione breve può corrispondere a più versetti. L’ascolto progressivo aggiunge contesto audio fino a un limite di 60 secondi e i risultati ambigui restano indicati come incerti. Si accetta un ascolto più lungo in cambio di maggiore contesto, senza forzare una risposta prematura.","story0Section2Title":"Eseguire inference fuori dall’event loop","story0Section2Text":"La fase di inference del modello viene eseguita al di fuori dell’event loop asincrono dell’API. I file sono limitati a 25 MB, con limiti di durata diversi per ciascuna modalità. Questi vincoli mantengono finite le richieste costose, mentre l’API supporta sia i file sia le sessioni dal microfono in diretta.","story0Section3Title":"Misurare un compito ben definito","story0Section3Text":"La valutazione offline del 5 settembre 2026 riporta il 97,31% in top-1 e il 99,10% in top-3 per il riconoscimento del recitatore su 781 clip riservate alla valutazione, con sure distinte per i profili e i test. I risultati descrivono quel benchmark sui recitatori; non misurano il riconoscimento dei versetti e non garantiscono prestazioni con qualsiasi microfono, rumore o registrazione.","story1Title":"Prosodia araba su un piccolo server CPU","story1Summary":"Un modello di vocalizzazione da 4.8 MB, rispetto dei segni vocalici presenti e limiti espliciti dell’analisi automatica.","story1Section0Title":"Adattare il modello alle risorse disponibili","story1Section0Text":"Qafiya affianca l’analisi della prosodia classica di PyArud a un modello libtashkeel ONNX incluso di circa 4.8 MB. La vocalizzazione viene eseguita localmente sulla CPU senza PyTorch, Transformers, GPU o server esterni per i modelli. Un solo Uvicorn worker condivide una sessione di inference limitata e serializzata, per controllare le copie del modello e le esecuzioni simultanee.","story1Section1Title":"Preservare il testo dell’autore","story1Section1Text":"I segni vocalici già presenti hanno la precedenza. La vocalizzazione automatica completa quelli mancanti e segnala le modifiche; l’interfaccia mostra il testo analizzato e conserva l’originale. La distinzione conta perché la scansione dipende dalla pronuncia e una vocale prevista può cambiare il risultato.","story1Section2Title":"Provare il container e dichiarare i limiti","story1Section2Text":"Il test locale documentato ha eseguito l’immagine di produzione con un carico sull’intera applicazione ASGI, entro limiti di 512 MiB di RAM e 0.1 CPU. Il process RSS ha raggiunto un picco di 142.55 MiB senza errori out-of-memory. È una misura su un carico limitato, non una garanzia per qualsiasi traffico pubblico. In un altro campione di 12 versi, le corrispondenze metriche dei testi parzialmente vocalizzati sono passate da 2/12 a 10/12; i testi completamente privi di segni vocalici hanno raggiunto solo 2/12.","story1Section3Title":"Limitare le revisioni e conservare il testo valido","story1Section3Text":"Il workflow sperimentale verifica il metro e il rawi richiesto, poi rivede i versi non validi con un ciclo limitato. Il backend preserva i versi accettati e gli emistichi corretti. L’uguaglianza del rawi non equivale alla verifica completa della rima classica e l’accettazione automatica non certifica la qualità letteraria. La generazione con AI resta disattivata nella demo pubblica.","notebookTitle":"Quaderno di ingegneria","readNote":"Leggi la nota tecnica","allNotes":"Torna alle note","noteLabel":"Nota tecnica","readingTime":"3 min di lettura","articleContext":"Un approfondimento sulle scelte tecniche e sui risultati documentati nel repository del progetto.","contentsLabel":"In questo articolo","sourcesTitle":"Fonti e implementazione","sourceReadme":"README del progetto","sourceEvidence":"Valutazione e risultati","exploreProject":"Esplora il progetto","continueReading":"Continua a leggere","writtenBy":"Di","writingTitle":"Le scelte tecniche, spiegate.","evidenceCaption":"Basato sul README del progetto e sulle valutazioni collegate.","copyLink":"Copia link","linkCopied":"Link copiato","writingKicker":"Quaderno di ingegneria","downloadCV":"Scarica il CV","contactIntent":"Cerco un ruolo a tempo pieno come sviluppatore Python per creare servizi backend affidabili e applicazioni di AI. Se è ciò che serve al tuo team, parliamone.","employmentDates":"Ingegnere del software · Lug. 2026 — Oggi","internshipDates":"In precedenza: tirocinio di fine studi presso SpeakDuo · Gen. — Lug. 2026.","achievementFeedback":"Ho sviluppato feedback multilingue su grammatica e pronuncia, generazione di lezioni e pratica personalizzata per la piattaforma in produzione.","achievementPractice":"Ho creato il monitoraggio del vocabolario, esercizi di spaced repetition e una valutazione CEFR basata su Elo per supportare l’apprendimento adattivo.","achievementVoice":"Ho implementato con LiveKit un voice agent multilingue per interviste e ottimizzato il processo di speech recognition per i sottotitoli in tempo reale tramite voice activity detection.","achievementMultiplayer":"Ho realizzato AI chat, pratica grammaticale personale e attività multiplayer sincronizzate nel backend e nell’applicazione web.","decisionsKicker":"SFIDE E COMPROMESSI","decisionsTitle":"Il perché delle scelte tecniche.","switchDark":"Attiva il tema scuro","switchLight":"Attiva il tema chiaro","opensNewTab":"Si apre in una nuova scheda","technologyLabel":"Tecnologie","contactLinksLabel":"Contatti e profili social","homeLabel":"Pagina iniziale di Taha Chelly","browseNotebook":"Sfoglia il quaderno","navNotebook":"Quaderno","sectionLink":"Link a questa sezione","projectSectionsLabel":"Sezioni del progetto","projectScreenshots":"Schermate","projectArchitecture":"Come funziona","projectDecisions":"Scelte tecniche"},"zh":{"languageLabel":"语言","navAbout":"关于","navWork":"工作","navContact":"联系","intro":"你好，我是 TAHA","heroTitle":"Taha Chelly。<br><span>软件工程师。</span><br>热爱创造。","heroDescription":"我开发实用的 AI 产品，将可靠的系统与直观易用的用户体验相结合。","connect":"联系我","github":"GitHub","currentlyAt":"目前就职于 <a href=\"#work\">SpeakDuo</a>","role":"软件工程师","portraitNote":"将想法转化为真实体验","aboutKicker":"关于我","aboutTitle":"代码背后的人。","aboutText":"我叫 Taha Chelly，是一名常驻突尼斯斯法克斯的软件工程师。我喜欢参与产品从构想到落地的全过程：打造清晰的界面、可靠的 backend，以及真正能解决问题的智能功能。","aboutDetail":"我毕业于软件工程专业，拥有使用 FastAPI、SQL 和 Docker 构建 Python backend、REST API 和 AI 应用的经验。我参与开发了 SpeakDuo 已投入生产的功能，并完成了端到端 AI 项目。我正在寻找全职 Python 开发岗位，希望构建可靠的 backend 服务，并在 AI engineering 领域持续成长。","tagFullStack":"全栈开发","tagAI":"AI 应用","tagRealtime":"实时体验","workKicker":"我正在做的事","workTitle":"有目标地创造。","current":"在职","workHeading":"帮助人们学好语言，<br>从一次次对话开始。","workDescription":"我负责 SpeakDuo 的 backend、Web 应用和语音代理，开发实时翻译、口语反馈、互动练习和个性化学习功能。","remote":"远程","toolkitTitle":"我使用的一些工具","contactKicker":"美好的想法始于一次交流","contactTitle":"一起做出<br><span>值得分享的作品。</span>","footerLine":"用心打造，不断进步。","backToTop":"返回顶部 ↑","navProjects":"项目","projectsKicker":"精选项目","projectsTitle":"让想法成为现实。","viewProject":"探索项目 ↗","projectCategory":"音频 · AI · WEB","projectSummary":"识别诵读者，查找正在聆听的经文。支持实时聆听和音频上传的《古兰经》诵读识别应用。","backProjects":"← 所有项目","liveDemo":"体验在线演示","sourceCode":"在 GitHub 上查看","screenshotsKicker":"应用截图","screenshotsTitle":"两种方式探索诵读。","reciterCaption":"诵读者识别：上传音频或实时聆听。","verseCaption":"经文查找：从诵读中找到章名和节号。","approachKicker":"工作原理","approachTitle":"从声音到识别结果。","reciterTitle":"识别诵读者","reciterDetail":"ECAPA-TDNN 模型生成 voice embedding，由 ONNX Runtime 执行 inference，再通过 cosine similarity 对 20 位诵读者的声纹档案进行匹配排序。","verseTitle":"查找经文","verseDetail":"针对《古兰经》优化的 Whisper 模型将阿拉伯语音频转为文字。规范化后的文本与 6,236 节经文进行比对。","contextTitle":"聆听更多上下文","contextDetail":"匹配不明确时，渐进式聆听会收集更多音频。不确定的结果会明确标注。","stackKicker":"技术栈","stackTitle":"项目背后的技术。","frontendDetail":"Frontend：使用 React 19 和 TypeScript，通过 Vite 和 Tailwind CSS 4 构建。浏览器录音和音频文件上传均通过 API 连接服务。","backendDetail":"Backend：使用 Python、FastAPI 和 WebSockets 实时识别诵读者。ONNX Runtime 计算 speaker embeddings；faster-whisper 和 CTranslate2 将诵读转写为文本。","deployDetail":"部署：在 Render 上运行 Docker containers，由 Nginx 提供 frontend 服务。GitHub Actions 检查 backend 和 frontend 后，再部署有变更的服务。","tryTitle":"聆听，发现。","qafiyaCategory":"语言 · 诗歌 · AI","qafiyaSummary":"阿拉伯诗歌工作坊：探索古典格律、押韵、韵律切分和本地元音符号补全。","qafiyaCaptionDesk":"写作空间：选择古典格律和押韵字母，再查看诗句的韵律。","qafiyaCaptionMobile":"适配手机的阿拉伯诗歌分析界面。","qafiyaApproachTitle":"从诗句到韵律。","qafiyaAnalysisTitle":"分析古典格律","qafiyaAnalysisDetail":"使用 PyArud，按照 16 种古典格律检查阿拉伯诗句。查看两个半句、用二进制表示的节律、音步和指定的押韵字母（rawi）。","qafiyaTashkeelTitle":"在本地补全元音符号","qafiyaTashkeelDetail":"内置的约 4.8 MB libtashkeel ONNX 模型在 CPU 上补全缺失的元音符号，保留已有标注；分析不会调用 LLM。","qafiyaDraftTitle":"诗歌生成仍处于实验阶段","qafiyaDraftDetail":"可选模型可生成诗句，并针对未通过的诗句进行修改，同时保留已通过内容。公开演示暂未启用生成。","qafiyaFrontend":"Frontend：React 19、TypeScript 和 Vite，提供支持 RTL 的响应式阿拉伯语界面。","qafiyaBackend":"Backend：Python 3.12、FastAPI、PyArud、NumPy 和 CPU 版 ONNX Runtime。单个 worker 共享使用受限的 inference session。","qafiyaDeploy":"托管：frontend 位于 Cloudflare Pages，Docker API 位于 Render。GitHub Actions 检查 frontend、backend 和生产 container。","qafiyaTryTitle":"探索格律与押韵。","generationPaused":"演示版可进行诗歌分析。AI 生成目前已关闭。","cvFormat":"PDF · 129 KB","story0Title":"当一段音频还不足以确定结果","story0Summary":"将诵读者识别与经文检索分开处理，并在聆听过程中明确呈现不确定性。","story0Section0Title":"两个问题，两条 pipeline","story0Section0Text":"识别诵读者与识别词语是两种不同的任务。Quranic Shazam 通过 ONNX Runtime 运行 ECAPA-TDNN，生成 speaker embeddings，并对 20 位诵读者的声纹档案进行匹配排序。经文检索则使用针对《古兰经》优化的 Whisper 模型，将阿拉伯语转写文本规范化后，与 6,236 节经文比对。speaker embeddings 模型以 pretrained 状态使用，并未使用《古兰经》录音进行 fine-tuning。","story0Section1Title":"先补充上下文，再判断是否足够确定","story0Section1Text":"一段简短的诵读可能对应多节经文。渐进式聆听会持续补充音频上下文，最长 60 秒，同时将模糊结果标记为不确定。这一设计用更长的聆听时间换取更多上下文，而不是强行提前给出答案。","story0Section2Title":"让 inference 在 event loop 之外运行","story0Section2Text":"模型 inference 在 API 的异步 event loop 之外执行。上传文件最大为 25 MB，各识别模式另有音频时长限制。这些边界控制了高成本请求的范围，同时让 API 支持文件上传和实时麦克风会话。","story0Section3Title":"明确评估的是哪一项任务","story0Section3Text":"2026 年 9 月 5 日的 offline 评估使用 781 段留出的测试音频，诵读者识别的 top-1 为 97.31%，top-3 为 99.10%。声纹档案与评估音频采用不同章节。这些结果仅描述该诵读者 benchmark，不代表经文识别准确率，也不能保证在任意麦克风、噪声或录音条件下的表现。","story1Title":"在小型 CPU 服务器上分析阿拉伯诗律","story1Summary":"约 4.8 MB 的元音标注模型、对已有元音符号的保留，以及自动分析能力的明确边界。","story1Section0Title":"让模型适应托管资源","story1Section0Text":"Qafiya 将 PyArud 的古典诗律分析与内置的约 4.8 MB libtashkeel ONNX 模型结合。元音标注在本地 CPU 上运行，无需 PyTorch、Transformers、GPU 或外部模型服务器。单个 Uvicorn worker 共享受限且串行执行的 inference session，以控制模型副本数量和并发执行。","story1Section1Title":"保留作者原有的文字","story1Section1Text":"已有的元音符号具有优先权。自动元音标注只补全缺失符号，并说明改动；界面显示实际分析的文本，同时保留原始输入。这一区别很重要，因为诗律切分取决于发音，一个预测的元音就可能改变分析结果。","story1Section2Title":"测试 container，并说明测试边界","story1Section2Text":"文档记录的本地测试在 512 MiB RAM、0.1 CPU 的限制下，对生产镜像运行覆盖整个 ASGI 应用的工作负载。process RSS 峰值为 142.55 MiB，未出现 out-of-memory。这是有界工作负载下的证据，不能保证任意公网流量下的表现。另一组 12 个诗句的元音标注样本中，部分标注文本的格律匹配由 2/12 提高到 10/12；完全未标注元音符号的文本仅达到 2/12。","story1Section3Title":"限制修订范围，保留有效诗句","story1Section3Text":"实验性 workflow 先检查格律与指定的 rawi，再通过有界循环修订未通过的诗句。backend 保留已接受的诗句和正确的半句。rawi 相同并不等于通过完整的古典押韵验证，机器接受也不能证明文学质量。公开演示仍未启用 AI 生成。","notebookTitle":"工程笔记","readNote":"阅读技术笔记","allNotes":"返回全部笔记","noteLabel":"技术笔记","readingTime":"阅读约 3 分钟","articleContext":"介绍项目 repository 中记录的实现决策与评估结果。","contentsLabel":"本文目录","sourcesTitle":"来源与实现","sourceReadme":"项目 README","sourceEvidence":"评估与依据","exploreProject":"查看项目","continueReading":"继续阅读","writtenBy":"作者","writingTitle":"解读技术决策。","evidenceCaption":"依据项目 README 及其链接的评估报告。","copyLink":"复制链接","linkCopied":"链接已复制","writingKicker":"工程笔记","downloadCV":"下载 CV","contactIntent":"我正在寻找全职 Python 开发岗位，希望构建可靠的 backend 服务和 AI 应用。如果这符合团队的需求，欢迎联系。","employmentDates":"软件工程师 · 2026 年 7 月至今","internshipDates":"此前：SpeakDuo 毕业实习 · 2026 年 1 月至 7 月。","achievementFeedback":"为已投入生产的平台开发多语言语法与发音反馈、课程生成和个性化练习。","achievementPractice":"开发词汇追踪、spaced repetition 练习以及基于 Elo 的 CEFR 评估，支持自适应学习。","achievementVoice":"使用 LiveKit 实现多语言面试 voice agent，并通过 voice activity detection 优化实时字幕的 speech recognition。","achievementMultiplayer":"跨 backend 和 Web 应用交付 AI chat、个人语法练习和同步 multiplayer 学习活动。","decisionsKicker":"挑战与取舍","decisionsTitle":"这些技术选择的原因。","switchDark":"切换到深色模式","switchLight":"切换到浅色模式","opensNewTab":"在新标签页中打开","technologyLabel":"技术","contactLinksLabel":"联系方式与社交账号","homeLabel":"Taha Chelly 首页","browseNotebook":"浏览工程笔记","navNotebook":"笔记","sectionLink":"此章节的链接","projectSectionsLabel":"项目章节","projectScreenshots":"截图","projectArchitecture":"工作原理","projectDecisions":"技术决策"},"ja":{"languageLabel":"言語","navAbout":"プロフィール","navWork":"仕事","navContact":"連絡先","intro":"こんにちは、タハです","heroTitle":"Taha Chelly。<br><span>ソフトウェアエンジニア。</span><br>ものづくりが好きです。","heroDescription":"信頼できるシステムと直感的な使いやすさを組み合わせ、役立つ AI 製品を開発しています。","connect":"連絡する","github":"GitHub","currentlyAt":"現在 <a href=\"#work\">SpeakDuo</a> に在籍","role":"ソフトウェアエンジニア","portraitNote":"アイデアを現実の体験に変える","aboutKicker":"少しだけ自己紹介","aboutTitle":"コードを書く人。","aboutText":"チュニジアのスファックスを拠点に活動するソフトウェアエンジニア、Taha Chellyです。わかりやすい画面、信頼できるbackend、そして本当に役立つ機能を形にするまで、製品づくりの全工程に携わるのが好きです。","aboutDetail":"ソフトウェア工学の学位を取得し、FastAPI、SQL、Docker を使った Python backend、REST API、AI アプリケーションの開発経験があります。SpeakDuo で本番稼働する機能の開発に貢献し、AI プロジェクトを一貫して構築してきました。信頼できる backend サービスを開発し、AI engineering の分野で成長できる、フルタイムの Python 開発職を探しています。","tagFullStack":"フルスタック開発","tagAI":"AIアプリケーション","tagRealtime":"リアルタイム体験","workKicker":"取り組んでいること","workTitle":"目的を持って作る。","current":"在籍中","workHeading":"会話を重ねながら、<br>言語学習をサポートします。","workDescription":"SpeakDuoのbackend、Webアプリ、音声エージェントを担当し、リアルタイム翻訳や発話へのフィードバック、対話型アクティビティ、個別練習を開発しています。","remote":"リモート","toolkitTitle":"使用しているツール","contactKicker":"良いアイデアは会話から","contactTitle":"誰かに話したくなるものを<br><span>一緒に作りましょう。</span>","footerLine":"丁寧に作り、進化を続けています。","backToTop":"ページ上部へ ↑","navProjects":"プロジェクト","projectsKicker":"制作したプロジェクト","projectsTitle":"アイデアを形に。","viewProject":"プロジェクトを見る ↗","projectCategory":"音声 · AI · WEB","projectSummary":"朗誦者と、今聞いている節を見つける。リアルタイムの音声入力とファイルアップロードに対応したクルアーン朗誦認識アプリ。","backProjects":"← プロジェクト一覧","liveDemo":"デモを試す","sourceCode":"GitHub で見る","screenshotsKicker":"アプリの画面","screenshotsTitle":"朗誦を探る、2つの方法。","reciterCaption":"朗誦者の認識：音声をアップロード、またはリアルタイムで入力。","verseCaption":"節の検索：朗誦から章と節を見つける。","approachKicker":"仕組み","approachTitle":"音声から、一致する朗誦へ。","reciterTitle":"朗誦者を識別","reciterDetail":"ECAPA-TDNN モデルが voice embedding を生成します。ONNX Runtime で inference を実行し、cosine similarity により20人の朗誦者のプロファイルとの一致度を順位付けします。","verseTitle":"節を見つける","verseDetail":"クルアーン向けに調整した Whisper がアラビア語音声を文字に変換。正規化したテキストを6,236節と照合します。","contextTitle":"さらに聞いて判断","contextDetail":"候補が曖昧な場合は、段階的に音声を追加して文脈を集めます。不確かな結果はその旨を表示します。","stackKicker":"技術スタック","stackTitle":"アプリを支える技術。","frontendDetail":"Frontend：React 19 と TypeScript を使い、Vite と Tailwind CSS 4 で構築しています。ブラウザーのマイク録音と音声ファイルのアップロードを API に接続します。","backendDetail":"Backend：Python と FastAPI を使い、WebSockets で朗誦者をリアルタイムに識別します。ONNX Runtime が speaker embeddings の計算を、faster-whisper と CTranslate2 が朗誦の文字起こしを担当します。","deployDetail":"デプロイ：Render 上の Docker containers と、frontend を配信する Nginx を使用します。GitHub Actions で backend と frontend を検証し、変更のあるサービスをデプロイします。","tryTitle":"聞いて、見つける。","qafiyaCategory":"言語 · 詩 · AI","qafiyaSummary":"アラビア詩の工房。古典韻律、脚韻、韻律分析、ローカルでの母音記号補完を試せます。","qafiyaCaptionDesk":"執筆画面 — 古典韻律と脚韻の基準となる文字を選び、詩句を分析します。","qafiyaCaptionMobile":"スマートフォンに対応したアラビア詩分析画面。","qafiyaApproachTitle":"書かれた詩句からリズムへ。","qafiyaAnalysisTitle":"古典韻律を分析","qafiyaAnalysisDetail":"PyArud を使い、16種類の古典韻律に照らしてアラビア詩を確認します。各半句、二進数で表したリズム、韻脚、指定した脚韻の基準文字（rawi）を調べられます。","qafiyaTashkeelTitle":"母音記号をローカルで補完","qafiyaTashkeelDetail":"内蔵の4.8 MB libtashkeel ONNXモデルがCPUで母音記号を補います。入力済みの記号を尊重し、分析ではLLMを呼び出しません。","qafiyaDraftTitle":"詩の生成は実験段階","qafiyaDraftDetail":"任意のプロバイダーが詩を作成し、合格した箇所を保ちながら不合格の句を修正します。公開デモでは生成を無効にしています。","qafiyaFrontend":"Frontend: React 19、TypeScript、Vite。レスポンシブなアラビア語RTL画面です。","qafiyaBackend":"Backend：Python 3.12、FastAPI、PyArud、NumPy、CPU 版 ONNX Runtime を使用します。単一の worker が、利用に上限を設けた inference session を共有します。","qafiyaDeploy":"ホスティング：frontend は Cloudflare Pages、Docker API は Render で稼働します。GitHub Actions で frontend、backend、本番 container を検証します。","qafiyaTryTitle":"韻律と脚韻を探る。","generationPaused":"ライブデモでは分析を利用できます。AI生成は現在無効です。","cvFormat":"PDF · 129 KB","story0Title":"短い音声だけでは判断できないとき","story0Summary":"朗誦者の識別と章句の検索を分け、不確かさを聴取の流れの中で伝える。","story0Section0Title":"2つの問いに、2つの pipeline","story0Section0Text":"声の識別と単語の認識は異なる課題です。Quranic Shazam は ONNX Runtime で ECAPA-TDNN の speaker embeddings を生成し、20人の朗誦者のプロファイルと照合して候補を順位付けします。一方、章句の検索にはクルアーン向けに調整した Whisper モデルを使い、アラビア語の転写を正規化して6,236節と比較します。speaker embeddings のモデルは pretrained の状態で利用しており、クルアーンの録音を使った fine-tuning は行っていません。","story0Section1Title":"確信を示す前に、文脈を増やす","story0Section1Text":"短い朗誦は複数の節に一致する場合があります。段階的な聴取で最大60秒まで音声の文脈を追加し、曖昧な結果には不確かであることを表示します。早い段階で答えを決めつけるのではなく、聴取時間を延ばして判断材料を増やす設計です。","story0Section2Title":"inference を event loop の外で実行する","story0Section2Text":"モデルの inference は API の非同期 event loop の外で実行します。アップロードは25 MBまでとし、認識モードごとに音声の長さにも上限を設けています。これにより処理負荷の高いリクエストを制限しながら、ファイルとライブマイクの両方に対応します。","story0Section3Title":"何を測った結果なのかを明確にする","story0Section3Text":"2026年9月5日の offline 評価では、評価用に分けた781クリップに対して、朗誦者識別の top-1 が97.31%、top-3 が99.10%でした。プロファイル作成用と評価用では異なる章を使っています。これはその朗誦者 benchmark の結果であり、章句認識の精度を測るものでも、あらゆるマイク、雑音、録音での性能を保証するものでもありません。","story1Title":"小さな CPU サーバーでアラビア詩の韻律を分析する","story1Summary":"約4.8 MBの母音記号補完モデル、入力済み記号の尊重、そして自動分析の明確な限界。","story1Section0Title":"利用できるリソースにモデルを合わせる","story1Section0Text":"Qafiya は PyArud による古典韻律分析と、同梱した約4.8 MBの libtashkeel ONNX モデルを組み合わせています。母音記号の補完は CPU 上でローカルに動作し、PyTorch、Transformers、GPU、外部のモデルサーバーを必要としません。単一の Uvicorn worker が、上限を設けて直列実行する inference session を共有し、モデルの複製と同時実行を抑えます。","story1Section1Title":"書き手が入力した本文を守る","story1Section1Text":"すでに入力された母音記号を優先します。自動補完は不足する記号を補い、変更内容を示します。画面には分析に使った本文を表示しつつ、元の入力も保持します。韻律分析は発音に依存するため、推定した母音が1つ変わるだけでも結果が変わり得ます。","story1Section2Title":"container を検証し、結果の範囲を示す","story1Section2Text":"文書化されたローカルテストでは、512 MiB RAM と0.1 CPUの上限を設け、本番イメージで ASGI アプリ全体を通すワークロードを実行しました。process RSS の最大値は142.55 MiBで、out-of-memory は発生しませんでした。これは限定した負荷での結果であり、任意の公開トラフィックでの動作保証ではありません。別の12詩句のサンプルでは、一部に母音記号がある入力の韻律一致が2/12から10/12に改善しましたが、記号がまったくない入力では2/12にとどまりました。","story1Section3Title":"修正回数を制限し、正しい部分を残す","story1Section3Text":"実験的な workflow は韻律と指定した rawi を検証し、不合格の詩句を回数制限付きのループで修正します。backend は合格した詩句と正しい半句を保持します。rawi の一致は古典脚韻の完全な検証ではなく、機械による合格判定も文学的な質を証明しません。公開デモでは AI 生成を引き続き無効にしています。","notebookTitle":"エンジニアリングノート","readNote":"技術ノートを読む","allNotes":"ノート一覧に戻る","noteLabel":"技術ノート","readingTime":"約3分で読めます","articleContext":"プロジェクトの repository に記録された実装上の判断と評価結果を解説します。","contentsLabel":"この記事の内容","sourcesTitle":"出典と実装","sourceReadme":"プロジェクト README","sourceEvidence":"評価と根拠","exploreProject":"プロジェクトを見る","continueReading":"続けて読む","writtenBy":"執筆","writingTitle":"技術的な判断と、その理由。","evidenceCaption":"プロジェクトの README とリンク先の評価資料に基づいています。","copyLink":"リンクをコピー","linkCopied":"リンクをコピーしました","writingKicker":"エンジニアリングノート","downloadCV":"CVをダウンロード","contactIntent":"信頼できる backend サービスと AI アプリケーションを開発できる、フルタイムの Python 開発職を探しています。チームのニーズに合いましたら、ぜひご連絡ください。","employmentDates":"ソフトウェアエンジニア · 2026年7月〜現在","internshipDates":"それ以前：SpeakDuo 卒業研究インターンシップ · 2026年1月〜7月。","achievementFeedback":"本番稼働するプラットフォーム向けに、多言語の文法・発音フィードバック、レッスン生成、個別練習を開発しました。","achievementPractice":"語彙の追跡、spaced repetition の練習、Elo に基づく CEFR 評価を構築し、適応型学習を支えました。","achievementVoice":"LiveKit で多言語面接の voice agent を実装し、voice activity detection によりリアルタイム字幕の speech recognition を最適化しました。","achievementMultiplayer":"backend と Web アプリを通して、AI chat、個人向け文法練習、同期する multiplayer 学習アクティビティを実装しました。","decisionsKicker":"課題とトレードオフ","decisionsTitle":"技術的な選択の理由。","switchDark":"ダークモードに切り替える","switchLight":"ライトモードに切り替える","opensNewTab":"新しいタブで開きます","technologyLabel":"技術","contactLinksLabel":"連絡先とソーシャルリンク","homeLabel":"Taha Chelly ホーム","browseNotebook":"ノート一覧を見る","navNotebook":"ノート","sectionLink":"このセクションへのリンク","projectSectionsLabel":"プロジェクトの構成","projectScreenshots":"画面","projectArchitecture":"仕組み","projectDecisions":"技術的な判断"}};
